<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Ablation Study</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate RADAC and RAFMAC with three risk distortions CVaR, Wang, and CPW under the same 1000‑step evaluation protocol used above.
Across seeds, Wang generally tilts updates toward higher means and weaker tails; CPW sits between CVaR and Wang but shows higher variance across seeds. Overall, CVaR is the most reliable choice for lower‑tail control at comparable mean.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Ablation (1000-step evaluation). RADAC/RAFMAC with CVaR, Wang, and CPW on <span id="A4.T5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">halfcheetah</span>-medium-replay and <span id="A4.T5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">walker2d</span>-medium-replay. Scores are mean <math id="A4.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> s.e. over 3 seeds.</figcaption>
