<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>2D Synthetic Task Details</h3>

<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Risky–Bandit dataset</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We generate <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> state–action–reward tuples with dummy zero states. Actions come from two modes:
(i) Ring (80%): radius <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9\pm 0.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9\pm 0.04</annotation></semantics></math>; base reward <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(9,\,0.3^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mn> 0.3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(9,\,0.3^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>; with probability <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math> a trap penalty <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-40</annotation></semantics></math> is applied (heavy lower tail).
(ii) Centre (20%): <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\,0.1^{2}\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mn> 0.1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\,0.1^{2}\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>; reward <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(5,\,0.3^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mn> 0.3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(5,\,0.3^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Actions are clipped to <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All methods train on the same static dataset; when a BC regulariser is required we use the standard loss of the underlying generator. RADAC adds the CVaR term from Eq. <a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 3.3 Behavior-regularized Objective ‣ 3 Risk-Aware Multimodal Actor-Critic (RAMAC) ‣ RAMAC: Multimodal Risk-Aware Offline Reinforcement Learning and the Role of Behavior Regularization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> to the diffusion/flow BC objective and backpropagates.
For each trained policy we draw <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> action samples for visualisation in Fig. <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4.3.3 Example Results ‣ 4.3 Example ‣ 4 Behavior Regularization ‣ RAMAC: Multimodal Risk-Aware Offline Reinforcement Learning and the Role of Behavior Regularization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Stochastic-D4RL MuJoCo Suite</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets</span> We adopt the <em id="A5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">stochastic MuJoCo</em> protocol for risk-sensitive offline RL, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Urpí et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. Policies are evaluated on</p>
<table id="A5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textsc{hopper},\ \textsc{walker2d},\ \textsc{halfcheetah}\}\ \times\ \{\textsc{medium-expert},\ \textsc{medium-replay}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">hopper</mtext><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">walker2d</mtext><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">halfcheetah</mtext><mo rspace="0.555em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">medium-expert</mtext><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">medium-replay</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textsc{hopper},\ \textsc{walker2d},\ \textsc{halfcheetah}\}\ \times\ \{\textsc{medium-expert},\ \textsc{medium-replay}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Compared to prior work, we prefer <span id="A5.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">medium-expert</span> and <span id="A5.SS2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">medium-replay</span> to validate both <em id="A5.SS2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">risk sensitivity</em> and <em id="A5.SS2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">policy expressiveness</em> under multimodal action distributions.
For training, we relabel per-transition rewards in the offline datasets to inject stochastic hazards
(velocity or torso-pitch thresholds with Bernoulli penalties and early termination);
<em id="A5.SS2.p1.2.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">the same hazard model is used at evaluation.</em>
This ensures the critic and the policy are trained on the risk-aware rewards rather than only being tested under hazards.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Settings</span> Each task defines a monitored signal and an additive Bernoulli penalty when a safety condition is violated; pose-based tasks also include an early-termination threshold.</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">HalfCheetah</span> : monitor forward velocity. Apply a penalty with probability <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.05</annotation></semantics></math> if the threshold is exceeded. Thresholds/penalties: <span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">medium-expert</span>/<span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">medium-replay</span> uses <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v&gt;10.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>10.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v&gt;10.0</annotation></semantics></math>/ <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v&gt;5.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>5.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v&gt;5.0</annotation></semantics></math> with penalty <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-70.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>70.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-70.0</annotation></semantics></math>. No early termination. Max episode steps: <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">Hopper<span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> / </span>Walker2D</span> : monitor torso pitch angle. When <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\theta|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\theta|</annotation></semantics></math> leaves the healthy range, add a penalty with probability <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.10</annotation></semantics></math>; terminate early if <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta&gt;2|\tilde{\theta}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta&gt;2|\tilde{\theta}|</annotation></semantics></math> . Max episode steps: <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">500</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A5.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.25em;">
<li id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Hopper</span>: healthy range <math id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-0.1,0.1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-0.1,0.1]</annotation></semantics></math> rad; penalty <math id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-50.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>50.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-50.0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\tilde{\theta}|&gt;0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\tilde{\theta}|&gt;0.1</annotation></semantics></math>; early termination if <math id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\theta|&gt;0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\theta|&gt;0.2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Walker2D</span>: healthy range <math id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-0.5,0.5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-0.5,0.5]</annotation></semantics></math> rad; penalty <math id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-30.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>30.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-30.0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\tilde{\theta}|&gt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\tilde{\theta}|&gt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math>; early termination if <math id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\theta|&gt;1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\theta|&gt;1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Baselines: Implementation &amp; Hyperparameters</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We include five representative offline-RL methods standard:</p>
<ul id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CODAC</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., 2021</a>)</cite> (distributional conservative learning). We primarily use the CVaR-optimizing specification (“CODAC-C”, <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CVaR}_{0.1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>CVaR</mi><mn>0.1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CVaR}_{0.1}</annotation></semantics></math> objective).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ORAAC</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Urpí et al., 2021</a>)</cite> (offline risk-averse actor–critic). A distributional critic with imitation-regularized policy optimizing a coherent risk objective.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CQL</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kumar et al., 2020</a>)</cite> (value pessimism). Non-distributional conservative Q-learning baseline.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DiffusionQL</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2023</a>)</cite> (expressive risk-neutral diffusion policy).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FlowQL</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Park et al., 2025</a>)</cite> (expressive risk-neutral flow-matching policy).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hyperparameter selection &amp; tuning</h5>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each of baselines, we run all baselines ourselves and tune the following parameters or adopt authors’ recommended settings, mirroring the practice in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al. (2021)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Urpí et al. (2021)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Park et al. (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kumar et al. (2020)</a></cite>.</p>
<ul id="A5.I3" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FlowQL</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Park et al., 2025</a>)</cite>: we sweep the policy weight <math id="A5.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\{1,10,30,100,1000\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\{1,10,30,100,1000\}</annotation></semantics></math> per task and report the best-performing setting (selection by <math id="A5.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CVaR}_{0.1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>CVaR</mi><mn>0.1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CVaR}_{0.1}</annotation></semantics></math> unless noted).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DiffusionQL</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>: we consider <math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in\{0.1,0.5,1.0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in\{0.1,0.5,1.0\}</annotation></semantics></math> for BC coefficient . we use authors’ recommended configuration for other parameters without retuning. We also used the best checkpoint of their model on each benchmark by following their protocol.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ORAAC</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Urpí et al., 2021</a>)</cite>: use the paper’s recommended configuration (distributional critic, risk level <math id="A5.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, anchor/prior regularization) without additional sweeps.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CODAC</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., 2021</a>)</cite>: use the paper’s tuned settings for D4RL (risk level <math id="A5.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>) without further tuning.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CQL</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kumar et al., 2020</a>)</cite>: use the standard conservative coefficient and implementation defaults for MuJoCo locomotion.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Estimating the OOD Visitation Rate with a 1 –NN Detector</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At evaluation time, we estimate the fraction of actions produced by a policy that fall outside the empirical action support of the offline dataset. This fraction is reported as the OOD action rate <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\text{act}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>act</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\text{act}}</annotation></semantics></math> in Sec. <a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Empirical Analysis of Theoretical Insights ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ RAMAC: Multimodal Risk-Aware Offline Reinforcement Learning and the Role of Behavior Regularization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>. Let <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\mathcal{D}}=\{a_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\mathcal{D}}=\{a_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of actions in the offline dataset (per task), and let <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Euclidean norm in action space.
In our MuJoCo tasks, actions are already scaled to <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math> per dimension; we therefore use <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> directly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each dataset action <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, compute its nearest neighbour among the other dataset actions and the associated distance</p>
<table id="A5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}\;=\;\min_{j\neq i}\,\|a_{i}-a_{j}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}\;=\;\min_{j\neq i}\,\|a_{i}-a_{j}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Define the robust scale</p>
<table id="A5.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{medNN}\;=\;\mathrm{median}\{d_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>medNN</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>median</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{medNN}\;=\;\mathrm{median}\{d_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We set the OOD threshold to <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau\,=\,\kappa\cdot\operatorname{medNN}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>medNN</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\,=\,\kappa\cdot\operatorname{medNN}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa{=}3</annotation></semantics></math> unless otherwise stated.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Label evaluation actions</h5>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\text{eval}}=\{a^{(\text{eval})}_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>eval</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\text{eval}}=\{a^{(\text{eval})}_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> be all actions emitted across evaluation rollouts (we use 5 seeds <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 10 episodes/seed by default).
For each <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{(\text{eval})}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>eval</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{(\text{eval})}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, compute its distance to the dataset action set</p>
<table id="A5.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{(\text{eval})}_{t}\;=\;\min_{i\in\{1,\dots,N\}}\|a^{(\text{eval})}_{t}-a_{i}\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>eval</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>eval</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{(\text{eval})}_{t}\;=\;\min_{i\in\{1,\dots,N\}}\|a^{(\text{eval})}_{t}-a_{i}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and assign the indicator</p>
<table id="A5.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{\text{OOD}}(a^{(\text{eval})}_{t})\;=\;\mathbb{I}\!\left\{d^{(\text{eval})}_{t}\;&gt;\;\tau\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mtext>OOD</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>eval</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mi>𝕀</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>eval</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{\text{OOD}}(a^{(\text{eval})}_{t})\;=\;\mathbb{I}\!\left\{d^{(\text{eval})}_{t}\;&gt;\;\tau\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In practice we compute <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{(\text{eval})}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>eval</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{(\text{eval})}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> via a KD–tree built on <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> (query time <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log N)</annotation></semantics></math> in low to moderate dimensions).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We define the OOD action rate as the per–action frequency</p>
<table id="A5.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\text{act}}\;=\;\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbf{1}_{\text{OOD}}(a^{(\text{eval})}_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>act</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mtext>OOD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>eval</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\text{act}}\;=\;\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbf{1}_{\text{OOD}}(a^{(\text{eval})}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We report the mean and standard error over 5 seeds. Because episodes may terminate early under the stochastic wrappers, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the actual number of executed timesteps (not a fixed horizon), which makes the rate comparable across seeds.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Confidence intervals</h5>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a seed–level rate <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> trials, we use a binomial approximation for the standard error <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,\mathrm{SE}=\sqrt{\hat{\varepsilon}(1-\hat{\varepsilon})/T}\," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>SE</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,\mathrm{SE}=\sqrt{\hat{\varepsilon}(1-\hat{\varepsilon})/T}\,</annotation></semantics></math> and report the across–seed mean <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> s.e.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span><span id="A5.T6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RAMAC: hyperparameters.</span>
We keep only the knobs that materially affect performance and stability. Values are our defaults; brackets show typical sweep ranges.</figcaption>
<table id="A5.T6.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A5.T6.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T6.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.4pt;padding-bottom:0.4pt;" colspan="2"><span id="A5.T6.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Global</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A5.T6.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T6.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.4pt;padding-bottom:0.4pt;">Discount <math id="A5.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A5.T6.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.4pt;padding-bottom:0.4pt;"><math id="A5.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.99</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.99</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T6.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T6.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.4pt;padding-bottom:0.4pt;">Batch size <math id="A5.T6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A5.T6.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.4pt;padding-bottom:0.4pt;"><math id="A5.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T6.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
